# Use COUI for UI

All app UI lives in `:app` and must use the `:coui` library (`com.coui.appcompat`).

- Theme screens with `Theme.COUI.Main.Light` / `Theme.COUI.Main.Dark` (or a style that parents those).
- Inflate COUI widgets (`COUISearchBar`, `COUIEmptyStateView`, COUI lists, buttons, dialogs, etc.).
- Prefer COUI attributes (`?attr/couiColorBackground`, `couiSearchBarStyle`) over Material or custom drawables.
- Set `viewInflaterClass` to `com.coui.appcompat.theme.COUIComponentsViewInflater` on the app theme.
- Do not add Material Design screens, AppCompat-only widgets, or custom lookalikes when a COUI widget exists.

```xml
<!-- BAD -->
<com.google.android.material.appbar.MaterialToolbar ... />

<!-- GOOD -->
<com.coui.appcompat.searchview.COUISearchBar
    app:searchHint="@string/search_hint" />
```
